  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Calculate $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
  "worked_solution": "We use the identity $\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
